/-!
# Periodic billiard trajectories and critical inscribed polygons

Let `χ` be an arclength parametrization of the boundary of a strictly convex billiard table
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable`), with period `L`, and let `β` be its billiard map on the
space `AddCircle L × (-1, 1)` of collision states
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.billiardMap`).
This file identifies the periodic orbits of `β` with the critical points of the cyclic discrete
action of the chord length, as an instance of the chain dictionary for generating functions
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`).

Minus the chord length, the generating function `S(s, t) = -‖χ(t) - χ(s)‖` of the billiard map
on the strip, is `L`-periodic in each argument, so it descends to the function

`S([s], [t]) = -‖χ(t) - χ(s)‖`

on the torus `AddCircle L × AddCircle L` of pairs of boundary parameters
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.circleGeneratingFunction`). It is differentiable off the
diagonal, where the two boundary points differ. Read the collision state `([s], v)` as the covector
`v ds` at `[s]` of the cotangent bundle of the circle `AddCircle L`, whose tangent lines are read in
its charts as `ℝ` (`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.stateCovector`). Then `S` generates the
billiard map in the sense of generating functions on manifolds: over the base pair `([s], [t])` of
a state and its image, the relation `p = d₁S`, `P = -d₂S` generated by `S` is the pair formed by
the state and its image
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.generatingCorrespondence_billiardMap`), and every off-diagonal
pair is such a base pair. This is the manifold form of the generating
identities `v = ∂_s S(s, t)` and `w = -∂_t S(s, t)` on the strip.

The chain dictionary then gives, for every `N ≥ 1`, a bijection between the marked `N`-periodic
billiard trajectories, that is the sequences of states `x_i`, `i ∈ ℤ/N`, with `β(x_i) = x_(i+1)`,
and the critical points of the cyclic action

`A_N(q_0, …, q_(N-1)) = Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))`

on the configurations with consecutive vertices distinct, by taking base points
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.exists_equiv_periodic_billiardMap`). The cyclic action is minus
the perimeter of the inscribed polygon with vertices `χ(q_i)`
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.cyclicAction_circleGeneratingFunction`), so its critical
points are the critical inscribed `N`-gons. Nonconsecutive vertices may coincide, and the least
period of the trajectory may be a proper divisor of `N`.

In terms of real lifts `s_k` of the vertices, a configuration with consecutive vertices distinct is
critical exactly when the equal-angle law of specular reflection holds at every vertex: the unit
vectors `u_(k-1)` and `u_k` along the incoming and outgoing chords have equal tangential components,
`⟪u_(k-1), χ'(s_k)⟫ = ⟪u_k, χ'(s_k)⟫`
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_circleGeneratingFunction_eq_zero_iff`).
Combined with the existence of such polygons by perimeter maximization
(`TauCeti.exists_billiard_periodic_reflection`), this shows that for every `N ≥ 2` the billiard map
has a point of period `N`, whose least period divides `N`
(`TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.exists_isPeriodicPt_billiardMap`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.circleGeneratingFunction`: minus the chord length, on pairs of
  points of the circle of boundary parameters.
* `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.stateCovector`: the collision state `([s], v)` as the covector
  `v ds` of the cotangent bundle of `AddCircle L`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.generatingCorrespondence_billiardMap`: the generating function
  `S` generates the billiard map.
* `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.exists_equiv_periodic_billiardMap`: marked `N`-periodic
  billiard trajectories correspond to critical inscribed `N`-gons.
* `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_circleGeneratingFunction_eq_zero_iff`:
  critical inscribed polygons are those obeying the equal-angle law at every vertex.
* `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.exists_isPeriodicPt_billiardMap`: the billiard map has a point
  of period `N` for every `N ≥ 2`.

## References

* Ana Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Sections 5.1 and 5.2 (periodic points of generated maps, and periodic billiard
  trajectories as critical inscribed polygons).
* Serge Tabachnikov, *Geometry and Billiards*, Student Mathematical Library 30, American
  Mathematical Society, 2005, Chapter 6 (periodic trajectories and Birkhoff's variational
  argument).
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Bundle Function Set
open scoped Manifold RealInnerProductSpace

namespace TauCeti

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [Fact (Module.finrank ℝ E = 2)]

namespace StrictConvexBilliardTable

variable {o : Orientation ℝ E (Fin 2)} (χ : StrictConvexBilliardTable o)

/-! ### The generating function on the circle -/

/-- The covectors `-((-a) ds)` and `b ds` on the real line agree exactly when `a = b`. -/
private theorem neg_smulRight_neg_eq_smulRight_iff (a b : ℝ) :
    -(1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (-a) = (1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight b ↔ a = b := by
  simp [ContinuousLinearMap.ext_ring_iff]

/-- The generating function `S([s], [t]) = -‖χ(t) - χ(s)‖` of the billiard map on pairs of points
of the circle `AddCircle L` of boundary parameters: minus the length of the chord from `χ(s)` to
`χ(t)`. It is the generating function `TauCeti.StrictConvexBilliardTable.generatingFunction` of the
strip, which is `L`-periodic in each argument. -/
def circleGeneratingFunction (x : AddCircle χ.period × AddCircle χ.period) : ℝ :=
  -‖χ.periodic.lift x.2 - χ.periodic.lift x.1‖

theorem circleGeneratingFunction_def (x : AddCircle χ.period × AddCircle χ.period) :
    χ.circleGeneratingFunction x = -‖χ.periodic.lift x.2 - χ.periodic.lift x.1‖ :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem circleGeneratingFunction_coe (s t : ℝ) :
    χ.circleGeneratingFunction ((s : AddCircle χ.period), (t : AddCircle χ.period)) =
      χ.generatingFunction s t := by
  simp [circleGeneratingFunction_def, generatingFunction_def]

/-- The generating function on the circle is differentiable off the diagonal. -/
theorem mdifferentiableAt_circleGeneratingFunction
    {x : AddCircle χ.period × AddCircle χ.period} (hx : x.1 ≠ x.2) :
    MDifferentiableAt (𝓘(ℝ).prod 𝓘(ℝ)) 𝓘(ℝ) χ.circleGeneratingFunction x := by
  obtain ⟨⟨s, t⟩, rfl⟩ := AddCircle.prodMap_coe_surjective (p := χ.period) (q := χ.period) x
  rw [← (AddCircle.isLocalDiffeomorph_prodMap_coe χ.period χ.period 1
    (s, t)).mdifferentiableAt_comp_iff one_ne_zero, mdifferentiableAt_iff_differentiableAt]
  have hne : χ t - χ s ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.2 fun h ↦ hx (χ.apply_eq_apply_iff.1 h.symm)
  have h₂ : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fun z : ℝ × ℝ ↦ χ z.2) (s, t) :=
    (χ.differentiableAt t).comp (s, t) differentiableAt_snd
  have h₁ : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fun z : ℝ × ℝ ↦ χ z.1) (s, t) :=
    (χ.differentiableAt s).comp (s, t) differentiableAt_fst
  exact (DifferentiableAt.norm ℝ (h₂.sub h₁) hne).neg

/-- The differential of `S` in its first argument at `([s], [t])`, read in the charts of the
circle, is `⟪χ'(s), u⟫` for the unit vector `u` along the chord from `χ(s)` to `χ(t)`. -/
theorem mvfderiv_circleGeneratingFunction_left {s t : ℝ} (h : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ) (fun a ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction (a, (t : AddCircle χ.period)))
        (s : AddCircle χ.period) = (1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight ⟪deriv χ s, χ.chordDir s t⟫ := by
  -- On real lifts the function is the generating function of the strip in its first argument.
  have hd : HasDerivAt ((fun a ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction (a, (t : AddCircle χ.period))) ∘
      ((↑) : ℝ → AddCircle χ.period)) ⟪deriv χ s, χ.chordDir s t⟫ s :=
    (χ.hasDerivAt_generatingFunction_left h).congr_of_eventuallyEq
      (Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun s' ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction_coe s' t)
  exact AddCircle.mvfderiv_eq_smulRight_of_hasDerivAt hd

/-- The differential of `S` in its second argument at `([s], [t])`, read in the charts of the
circle, is `-⟪χ'(t), u⟫` for the unit vector `u` along the chord from `χ(s)` to `χ(t)`. -/
theorem mvfderiv_circleGeneratingFunction_right {s t : ℝ} (h : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ) (fun b ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction ((s : AddCircle χ.period), b))
        (t : AddCircle χ.period) = (1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (-⟪deriv χ t, χ.chordDir s t⟫) := by
  -- On real lifts the function is the generating function of the strip in its second argument.
  have hd : HasDerivAt ((fun b ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction ((s : AddCircle χ.period), b)) ∘
      ((↑) : ℝ → AddCircle χ.period)) (-⟪deriv χ t, χ.chordDir s t⟫) t :=
    (χ.hasDerivAt_generatingFunction_right h).congr_of_eventuallyEq
      (Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun t' ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction_coe s t')
  exact AddCircle.mvfderiv_eq_smulRight_of_hasDerivAt hd

/-! ### Collision states as covectors -/

/-- The collision state `([s], v)` as the covector `v ds` at `[s]` of the cotangent bundle of the
circle `AddCircle L` of boundary parameters, whose tangent lines are read in its charts as `ℝ`. The
tangential component `v` of the outgoing velocity is the canonical momentum conjugate to the
arclength parameter `s`. -/
def stateCovector (x : AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1) :
    CotangentBundle 𝓘(ℝ) (AddCircle χ.period) :=
  TotalSpace.mk' (ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ) x.1 ((1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (x.2 : ℝ))

@[simp]
theorem proj_stateCovector (x : AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1) :
    (χ.stateCovector x).proj = x.1 :=
  (rfl)

/-- The covector `v ds` of a collision state `([s], v)` takes the value `u * v` on the tangent
vector `u`. -/
@[simp]
theorem stateCovector_snd_apply (x : AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1) (u : ℝ) :
    (χ.stateCovector x).snd u = u * x.2 :=
  -- The fibre `TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ) [s] →L[ℝ] ℝ` is `ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ` by definition; the value is `u • v`.
  (rfl)

theorem stateCovector_injective : Injective χ.stateCovector := fun x y h ↦ by
  have h₁ : x.1 = y.1 := congrArg TotalSpace.proj h
  have h₂ : (x.2 : ℝ) = y.2 := by
    rw [← one_mul (x.2 : ℝ), ← one_mul (y.2 : ℝ), ← χ.stateCovector_snd_apply x,
      ← χ.stateCovector_snd_apply y, h]
  exact Prod.ext h₁ (Subtype.ext h₂)

/-! ### The billiard map is generated by the chord length -/

/-- Every pair of distinct points of the circle of boundary parameters is the base pair of a
collision state and its image under the billiard map. -/
theorem exists_fst_eq_and_fst_billiardMap_eq {a b : AddCircle χ.period} (h : a ≠ b) :
    ∃ x, x.1 = a ∧ (χ.billiardMap x).1 = b := by
  induction a using QuotientAddGroup.induction_on with | H s => ?_
  -- Lift `b` into the window `(s, s + L)`; it is not `s`, since `b ≠ [s]`.
  set t := AddCircle.equivIco χ.period s b
  have ht : (t : ℝ) ∈ Ioo s (s + χ.period) := ⟨lt_of_le_of_ne t.property.1 fun hst ↦
    h ((congrArg ((↑) : ℝ → AddCircle χ.period) hst).trans AddCircle.coe_equivIco), t.property.2⟩
  refine ⟨((s : AddCircle χ.period), ⟨_, χ.inner_deriv_chordDir_mem_Ioo s t⟩), rfl, ?_⟩
  rw [billiardMap_coe, χ.nextParam_inner_deriv_chordDir ht, AddCircle.coe_equivIco]

/-- **The chord length generates the billiard map.** Over the base pair `([s], [t])` of a collision
state `x = ([s], v)` and its image `β(x) = ([t], w)`, the cotangent relation `p = d₁S`, `P = -d₂S`
generated by `S([s], [t]) = -‖χ(t) - χ(s)‖` is the pair of covectors `(v ds, w dt)` of `x` and
`β(x)`. -/
theorem generatingCorrespondence_billiardMap (x : AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1) :
    CotangentBundle.generatingCorrespondence 𝓘(ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ) χ.circleGeneratingFunction
        (x.1, (χ.billiardMap x).1) = (χ.stateCovector x, χ.stateCovector (χ.billiardMap x)) := by
  obtain ⟨θ, v⟩ := x
  induction θ using QuotientAddGroup.induction_on with | H s => ?_
  have hne := χ.apply_nextParam_ne (s := s) v.property
  rw [billiardMap_coe, CotangentBundle.generatingCorrespondence_apply]
  refine Prod.ext (CotangentBundle.ext (by simp) fun u ↦ ?_)
    (CotangentBundle.ext (by simp) fun u ↦ ?_)
  · -- The first covector is `∂_s S(s, t) = v`.
    rw [CotangentBundle.generatingSource_snd]
    simp only
    rw [χ.mvfderiv_circleGeneratingFunction_left hne, χ.inner_deriv_chordDir_nextParam v.property]
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (χ.stateCovector_snd_apply _ u).symm
    -- The tangent line is `ℝ` by definition, and `(1.smulRight v) u = u • v`.
    rfl
  · -- The second covector is `-∂_t S(s, t) = w`.
    rw [CotangentBundle.generatingTarget_snd]
    simp only
    rw [χ.mvfderiv_circleGeneratingFunction_right hne, χ.chordDir_nextParam v.property]
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (χ.stateCovector_snd_apply _ u).symm
    simp only [nextTangential_def, real_inner_comm]
    -- The tangent line is `ℝ` by definition, and `(1.smulRight w) u = u • w`.
    exact congrArg (fun f : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ ↦ f u) ((neg_smulRight_neg_eq_smulRight_iff _ _).2 rfl)

/-! ### Periodic trajectories and critical inscribed polygons -/

/-- The cyclic discrete action `Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))` of the chord length is minus the perimeter of
the inscribed polygon with vertices `χ(q_i)`. -/
theorem cyclicAction_circleGeneratingFunction {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] (q : ZMod N → AddCircle χ.period) :
    cyclicAction (fun _ ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction) q =
      -inscribedPerimeter χ.periodic.lift q := by
  simp [cyclicAction_apply, inscribedPerimeter_def, circleGeneratingFunction_def]

/-- **Periodic billiard trajectories are critical inscribed polygons.** For `N ≥ 1`, taking base
points is a bijection from the marked `N`-periodic billiard trajectories, the sequences of collision
states `x_i`, `i ∈ ℤ/N`, with `β(x_i) = x_(i+1)`, onto the critical points of the cyclic action
`A_N(q) = Σ_i S(q_i, q_(i+1))`, minus the perimeter of the inscribed polygon, among the
configurations of `N` points of the circle of boundary parameters with consecutive points distinct.
Its inverse sends a critical configuration to the states whose covectors are the source points
`(q_i, d₁S(q_i, q_(i+1)))` of the relation generated by `S`. -/
theorem exists_equiv_periodic_billiardMap (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] :
    ∃ e : {x : ZMod N → AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1 //
          ∀ i, χ.billiardMap (x i) = x (i + 1)} ≃
        {q : ZMod N → AddCircle χ.period // (∀ i, q i ≠ q (i + 1)) ∧
          mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ 𝓘(ℝ))
            (cyclicAction fun _ ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction) q = 0},
      (∀ x i, (e x : ZMod N → AddCircle χ.period) i = (x.val i).1) ∧
        ∀ q i, χ.stateCovector ((e.symm q : ZMod N → AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1) i) =
          CotangentBundle.generatingSource 𝓘(ℝ) χ.circleGeneratingFunction
            (q.val i, q.val (i + 1)) := by
  classical
  -- The billiard map, transported to the covectors of collision states.
  let φ (z : CotangentBundle 𝓘(ℝ) (AddCircle χ.period)) :
      CotangentBundle 𝓘(ℝ) (AddCircle χ.period) :=
    if h : ∃ x, χ.stateCovector x = z then χ.stateCovector (χ.billiardMap h.choose) else z
  have hφ (x : AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1) :
      φ (χ.stateCovector x) = χ.stateCovector (χ.billiardMap x) := by
    have h : ∃ y, χ.stateCovector y = χ.stateCovector x := ⟨x, rfl⟩
    simp only [φ, h, ↓reduceDIte, χ.stateCovector_injective h.choose_spec]
  obtain ⟨e₀, he₀, he₀'⟩ := CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating (N := N)
    (S := fun _ ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction) (W := fun _ ↦ {x | x.1 ≠ x.2})
    (D := fun _ ↦ range χ.stateCovector) (φ := fun _ ↦ φ)
    (fun _ _ hx ↦ χ.mdifferentiableAt_circleGeneratingFunction hx)
    (fun _ z ↦ by
      rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩
      rw [hφ]
      exact ⟨Ne.symm (χ.fst_billiardMap_ne x), χ.generatingCorrespondence_billiardMap x⟩)
    (fun _ x hx ↦ by
      obtain ⟨y, hy₁, hy₂⟩ := χ.exists_fst_eq_and_fst_billiardMap_eq hx
      exact ⟨χ.stateCovector y, ⟨y, rfl⟩, by rw [hφ]; exact Prod.ext hy₁ hy₂⟩)
  -- Periodic trajectories of states are the periodic chains of their covectors.
  let e₁ : {x : ZMod N → AddCircle χ.period × Ioo (-1 : ℝ) 1 //
        ∀ i, χ.billiardMap (x i) = x (i + 1)} ≃
      {z : ZMod N → CotangentBundle 𝓘(ℝ) (AddCircle χ.period) //
        ∀ i, z i ∈ range χ.stateCovector ∧ φ (z i) = z (i + 1)} :=
    { toFun := fun x ↦ ⟨fun i ↦ χ.stateCovector (x.val i), fun i ↦ ⟨⟨_, rfl⟩, by rw [hφ,
        x.property i]⟩⟩
      invFun := fun z ↦ ⟨fun i ↦ (z.property i).1.choose, fun i ↦ χ.stateCovector_injective <| by
        rw [← hφ, (z.property i).1.choose_spec, (z.property i).2, (z.property
            (i + 1)).1.choose_spec]⟩
      left_inv := fun x ↦ Subtype.ext <| funext fun i ↦ χ.stateCovector_injective <|
        Exists.choose_spec (p := fun y ↦ χ.stateCovector y = χ.stateCovector (x.val i)) ⟨x.val i,
            rfl⟩
      right_inv := fun z ↦ Subtype.ext <| funext fun i ↦ (z.property i).1.choose_spec }
  refine ⟨e₁.trans e₀, fun x i ↦ he₀ _ i, fun q i ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [← he₀' q i]
  exact congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val (e₁.apply_symm_apply (e₀.symm q))) i

/-- **The equal-angle law at a critical inscribed polygon.** Let `s_k`, `k ∈ ℤ/N`, be boundary
parameters with consecutive boundary points `χ(s_k)` and `χ(s_(k+1))` distinct, and let `u_k` be the
unit vector along the chord from `χ(s_k)` to `χ(s_(k+1))`. The configuration `([s_k])` is a critical
point of the cyclic action of the chord length exactly when at every vertex the incoming and the
outgoing chords have equal tangential components, `⟪u_(k-1), χ'(s_k)⟫ = ⟪u_k, χ'(s_k)⟫`: the law of
specular reflection. -/
theorem mvfderiv_cyclicAction_circleGeneratingFunction_eq_zero_iff {N : ℕ} [NeZero N]
    {s : ZMod N → ℝ} (hs : ∀ k, χ (s (k + 1)) ≠ χ (s k)) :
    mvfderiv (ModelWithCorners.pi fun _ : ZMod N ↦ 𝓘(ℝ))
        (cyclicAction fun _ ↦ χ.circleGeneratingFunction)
        (fun k ↦ (s k : AddCircle χ.period)) = 0 ↔
      ∀ k, ⟪χ.chordDir (s (k - 1)) (s k), deriv χ (s k)⟫ =
        ⟪χ.chordDir (s k) (s (k + 1)), deriv χ (s k)⟫ := by
  rw [CotangentBundle.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_eq_zero_iff (q := fun k ↦ (s k : AddCircle χ.period))
    fun k ↦ χ.mdifferentiableAt_circleGeneratingFunction fun h ↦
      hs k (χ.apply_eq_apply_iff.2 h).symm]
  refine forall_congr' fun k ↦ ?_
  have hk : χ (s k) ≠ χ (s (k - 1)) := by simpa only [sub_add_cancel] using hs (k - 1)
  rw [CotangentBundle.generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq,
    χ.mvfderiv_circleGeneratingFunction_right hk, χ.mvfderiv_circleGeneratingFunction_left (hs k),
    real_inner_comm (χ.chordDir _ _), real_inner_comm (χ.chordDir _ _)]
  -- Both covectors are multiples of the unit covector `ds`.
  exact neg_smulRight_neg_eq_smulRight_iff _ _

/-- **Periodic billiard trajectories exist.** For every `N ≥ 2` the billiard map of a strictly
convex table has a point of period `N`, whose least period divides `N`. -/
theorem exists_isPeriodicPt_billiardMap {N : ℕ} (hN : 2 ≤ N) :
    ∃ x, IsPeriodicPt χ.billiardMap N x := by
  have : NeZero N := ⟨by omega⟩
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_billiard_periodic_reflection (χ := χ) χ.periodic χ.period_pos.ne'
    (fun t h ↦ by simpa [h] using χ.norm_deriv t) hN
  -- The vertices of a perimeter maximizer form a critical configuration of the cyclic action.
  have hcrit := (χ.mvfderiv_cyclicAction_circleGeneratingFunction_eq_zero_iff
    fun k ↦ (hs k).1).2 fun k ↦ by
      simpa only [chordDir_def, NormedSpace.normalize] using (hs k).2
  obtain ⟨e, -, -⟩ := χ.exists_equiv_periodic_billiardMap N
  set x := e.symm ⟨fun k ↦ (s k : AddCircle χ.period), fun k h ↦
    (hs k).1 (χ.apply_eq_apply_iff.2 h).symm, hcrit⟩
  -- Along the periodic trajectory, the `n`-th iterate of the billiard map moves `x_0` to `x_n`.
  have hiter (n : ℕ) : χ.billiardMap^[n] (x.val 0) = x.val n := by
    induction n with
    | zero => simp
    | succ n ih => rw [iterate_succ_apply', ih, x.property, Nat.cast_succ]
  exact ⟨x.val 0, (hiter N).trans (by rw [ZMod.natCast_self])⟩

end StrictConvexBilliardTable

end TauCeti
